	ü What is JS?

	• It is High Level interpreted programming language 
	• It is case sensitive 
	• It supports Object Oriented Programming and functional oriented programming 
	• It is dynamically typed language that is we never declare the data type upfront the engine figures it out at runtime 

	ü What is Node js ?

	• It is opensource cross platform runtime that let javascript to run outside the browser mainly on servers 

	ü What is the role of JS Engine ?

	• It is the one responsible to execute the JS code 

	• It converts the JS CODE to first byte code and then converts the byte code to binary code 

	• And because of Byte code JavaScript is platform independent 

	• JS CODE -----> Byte Code ------> Binary Code 

	ü What is npm ?

	• It stands for node package manager 
It is the one responsible for installing libraries for Javascript 
